    ""banana"": ""bænənɑ"",
    ""orange"": ""ɔrəŋə""
}
```
Note that the IPA phonetic representations are just one example of how you might represent the sounds of a word using ASCII characters. There are many other ways to do this, and different languages have different conventions for representing phonetic information in writing.']",0,[0],[],False,2,0,0,"[{""block_id"": 1, ""language"": ""unknown"", ""error"": ""Unsupported language: unknown""}, {""block_id"": 2, ""language"": ""unknown"", ""error"": ""Unsupported language: unknown""}]"

