This code creates a TCP/IP socket listener on port 8080, which listens for incoming client connections. When a client connects, it accepts the connection asynchronously using `AcceptTcpClientAsync()` and processes it in a separate task using `ProcessClientConnection()`. The method reads data from the network stream in chunks using `ReadAsync()` and processes them until no more data is available. Once done, it closes the client connection and moves on to the next one.

The `ProcessClientConnection()` method uses asynchronous I/O operations to read data in chunks from the network stream. It utilizes an event-driven mechanism that begins reading data upon successful reception and then restarts reading after processing each chunk. This approach ensures that the server can handle multiple client connections simultaneously without compromising performance.

